+//! Snapshots the terrain COLOUR tiles and the surface type (layer id) blocks that the normalised square
+//! (fpx +- radius, fpy +- radius) touches, and records them as ONE undo object in the currently open undo
+//! group. fpx / fpy / radius are in the same 0..1 whole-terrain measure the painter uses, i.e. fpx is the
+//! world Y axis and fpy is the world X axis (the CHeightmap swap).
+//!
+//! It exists so that a caller which writes CRGBLayer and the layer bitmap by hand - the terrain plate
+//! appearance commit - gets exactly the undo the texture painter gets for a dab, out of exactly the same
+//! objects (CUndoTPElement / CUndoTexturePainter, this file), instead of inventing a second one. Must be
+//! called BEFORE the writes and inside an open CUndo scope.
+void RecordTerrainAppearanceUndo(float fpx, float fpy, float radius);
